<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RMP Props yr pre-exceps shr slides, div off.</title>
<headline>RMP Props yr pre-exceps shr slides, div off.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre-exceps	    146	   vs 193</p>
<p>    - post exceps	   293	   vs 413</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 120	   vs 140</p>
<p>    Pre-exceps income     22.82	 vs 30.10</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   66.30	 vs 92.74</p>
<p>    Tax			 13.70	 vs 15.67</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   49.12	 vs 44.94</p>
<p>    Turnover		  292.46	vs 286.10</p>
<p>Div payable Jan 3</p>
<p>on register Nov 29</p>
<p>Full name: RMP Properties Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     26.51	 vs 43.98</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said exceptional items consisted of the balance of the net surplus arising from the sale of investment properties and a provision for the permanent decline of specific investment properties.</p>
<p>They said the group was set to improve its performance in the 1996/97 year provided business confidence and economic growth made the environment conducive to property investment.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
